# Third-party VT conformance vectors, hex-encoded.
# Provenance, and why byte 0 is dropped when replaying: PROVENANCE.md
#
# Format: <name> <sha256-of-decoded-bytes> <hex>
#
# Hex rather than the raw files, because the raw files are full of ESC and
# NUL and tools/leak-scan.sh refuses to pass a repository holding tracked
# binaries it cannot read. That refusal is right and this is the encoding
# the capture registry already asks in-repo fixtures to use.
#
# The bytes are unchanged. The digest on each line is over the DECODED
# content and is the same one recorded beside that vector's golden frame,
# so the encoding is checkable rather than trusted.

